WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.630
John: Hank, I'm here with the lovely Cara
Delevingne.

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.659
Cara: And I'm here with lovely John Green.

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:05.120
John: That was a pretty good imitation.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.120
Cara: I know.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.680
John: You play Margo in the movie and I'm
gonna ask you real questions by real nerdfighters.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.799
What's it like to kiss Nat?

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:11.799
Cara: Oh.

00:00:11.799 --> 00:00:14.150
*laughs* Yeah, he's a good kisser.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:16.240
He's a really good kisser.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.951
I was actually talking about him with a friend
of mine who's also kissed him.

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:22.160
And we had a whole conversation about how
he was a good kisser.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.160
Surprisingly good!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.390
John: I wonder what friend that could be.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.390
Cara: *shhhhh*

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.390
John: I'm just kidding I know.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.390
Cara: Do you?

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.390
John: Yeah.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.850
Is Margo someone that you can relate to?

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:30.850
And how?

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:31.850
Cara: Very much so.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:35.410
I think that's why I got the part because
a lot of the stories that she went through

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.940
in the book and all those kind of things,
I've been through before and a lot of the

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.500
lines they've actually written in the script
I've said before.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.310
She runs on instinct.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.079
She does what she feels in the moment and
doesn't really think about the consequences.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:48.079
John: And you're like that too.

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:49.079
Cara: Yeah.

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:50.079
John: Are you an octopus?

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:51.079
Cara: Obviously.

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:52.600
John: Is John a good executive producer?

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.600
Cara: No.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.600
John: It's true.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.600
Cara: *laughs* He is.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.600
John: What do I do as an executive producer?

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.290
Cara: You are so fun.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.290
*laughs*

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.831
John: What is John like in real life?

00:01:00.831 --> 00:01:02.120
Is he just like in the videos?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.320
Cara: I would say so.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.590
Yeah, you're... but I think you're even funnier
in real life, because you edit out all the

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.590
beautifulness.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.799
John: I knew a face touch was coming.

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:14.890
I knew I wasn't gonna get out of this video
without some kind of face touch.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:15.890
Bacon or Nutella?

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:16.890
Cara: That's so hard.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.890
Both.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:18.890
John: What is your opinion of my eyebrows?

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.460
Cara: I thought they'd be less coarse and
they're actually nice.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.010
They're good, they're a good texture.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.740
John: But they're not as good as yours.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:25.740
Cara: What?

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.030
John: Well I mean, you have famous eyebrows.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:29.030
Literally.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.210
You maybe have the most famous eyebrows on
Earth right now.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.210
Cara: No.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.210
John: Who?

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.110
Yeah you can't even think of someone.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.110
It's you!

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.310
Have you read the book Paper Towns?

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:38.310
Cara: No.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.310
John: Yes you have.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.370
Cara: Of course I have.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.530
It was really good.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.530
I really liked it.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.970
I didn't actually...yeah, I didn't know how
good you were.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:46.970
*laughs*

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:47.970
John: *laughs* Thanks man.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.810
Cara: I thought you were gonna be - not to
be rude - but like younger because you do

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.920
it from a young person's perspective so well.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.380
John: But I am in fact really old.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.380
Cara: You are.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.799
John: What is your favorite word?

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:01.420
Cara: My favorite word and my least favorite
word in one is regime.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.920
John: How did you feel when you found out
you'd been cast for this?

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:04.920
Cara: I cried.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.369
I remember where I was, like the whole thing.

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:07.890
I just remember freaking the freak out.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:08.890
John: Where were you?

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:13.130
Cara: I was actually by myself, which is a
bit sad, but I was in a hotel room getting

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.630
ready for work, and I got called, and I just
started crying.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.630
It was too much.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.580
John: I knew that you were gonna get it from
when I watched your audition.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.580
Cara: Really?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.580
John: Yeah.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.580
Cara: That's so nice.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.090
John: What do you want to be when you grow
up?

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.090
Cara: President.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.090
Prime Minister.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.090
An astronaut!

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.240
John: An astronaut Prime Minister.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:38.230
Cara: An alien-fighting Princess Peach with
steroid injecting angel gun with wings.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.230
On a unicorn!

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.230
Multi-colored.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.720
With golden eyes.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.620
John: That's good.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.880
That's detailed.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.650
Someone is gonna draw that.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.200
Cara: I hope so.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.890
Oh I want to be a lion slash monkey.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.660
John: Describe your friend Nat Wolff in three
words.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.069
Cara: Rambunctious.

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:56.490
John: Yup.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:57.910
Cara: Delicious.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.330
John: Agree.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.730
Cara: And nutritious.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.470
John: Strongly agree.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.470
Yeah.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.470
Cara: Totally.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.739
John: He's good to be around.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:06.780
Cara: And funny too.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.550
John: But not... he's less funny than he is
nutritious.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.769
Cara: Yeah, I agree.

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:15.400
John: Would you rather the world contain a
puppy-sized elephant or an elephant-sized

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.400
puppy?

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.400
Cara: A puppy-sized elephant.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.400
John: Yes!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.400
Cara: Obviously.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.400
John: What's your favorite fruit?

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.400
Cara: Passion fruit.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.490
John: What is your favorite color?

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.800
Cara: Periwinkle blue.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.190
John: And what is the meaning of life?

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:28.599
Cara: Love.

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:29.959
John: Thanks Cara.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:31.610
Thanks for being in my video.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.610
Cara: Thanks John.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:33.610
John: So there you have it Hank.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:34.830
Cara Delevingne likes my eyebrows and is an
octopus.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:38.090
It occurs to me that I forgot to say "Good
Morning" to you in this video so Good Morning,

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.340
it's actually nighttime, but Good Morning!

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.490
And now having said that, I will see you on
Friday, when the Project for Awesome begins!

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.660
Links in the doobly-doo to all the Project
for Awesome stuff!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.660
I'm so excited!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:46.661
Goodbye!

